  "verbalization": "Arillanin A is shown to interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1, which is a key enzyme in the glucuronidation of various compounds, including potential drug substrates. This enzyme is then targeted by CDAISMWEOUEBRE-LKPKBOIGSA-N, a protein that likely plays a role in the metabolic processing of arillanin A. The final pathway leads to the enzyme A2780cisR, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Arillanin A may influence the expression or activity of A2780cisR. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic link between Arillanin A and A2780cisR through the UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1 pathway, with the involvement of a second intermediate protein that may modulate the interaction. The scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further validation would be needed to confirm the exact role of the intermediate protein in the pathway.",
